WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:41.240
[Music]

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.080
[Narrator:] This is Captain Kimberly, our
Medical Officer.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.280
And these are some of our men eating their
evening meal,

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.600
as usual, at the end of another routine day.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.280
Yes, everything seems to be going well, just another day.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.620
But believe me, what followed

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.240
turned out to be anything but routine.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.480
This meal is the beginning of our story,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.920
a story that developed during the night

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.180
and continued for several days.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.520
During the early part of the night,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.140
we all went about our duties as usual.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.840
[Music]

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.760
Everything was nice and smooth and quiet,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.720
the way we like to see things run.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.500
At midnight, about 40 of us in the duty section got a light meal.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.340
It was just about this time that things were beginning to happen.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.720
It began like this.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.360
At first a few of the men who weren't in the duty section got sick.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.940
More followed suit.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.300
And just before dawn,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.440
most of the men who had the midnight meal
joined their ranks.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.280
You never saw such a sick bunch of men in
your life.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:21.900
And it got steadily worse: vomiting, abdominal
pains, and diarrhea.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.980
It was hard to tell which caused the most
trouble.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.880
One thing is sure, the boys were well taken
care of,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.140
some of them at the base infirmary,

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.580
and others at a private hospital in town.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:03:09.440
[Music]

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.800
For a while all we had time to do was bring
in the sick--

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.640
and some of them were plenty sick--

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.160
get them in bed,

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.080
and leave them to Captain Kimberly and his
assistants.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:36.720
[Music]

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.500
It was pretty rough going for a while.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:44.840
Vomiting, diarrhea, cramps, headache, sweating,

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.260
prostration, fever, and dehydration.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.680
Yes, salmonella can make you plenty sick.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:04:02.360
[Music]

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.980
Just as soon as we got the chance to let up
and breathe a little,

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.860
we got down to the business of finding

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.860
the cause of all the trouble.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.220
Naturally, we had suspected some kind of food
poisoning.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.020
And so it was.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.080
Look here, this is what we found.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:23.720
These are salmonella organisms of the species
typhimurium,

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.000
which were isolated from a patient's stool
specimen.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.280
From the lapse of time between our patient's last meal

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.320
and the outbreak of illness, it was pretty evident that the evening meals

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.060
were responsible for the presence

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.140
of the salmonella organisms in the stool specimen.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.620
In the meantime, our laboratory was working
on samples

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.540
of food eaten that night.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:05:01.020
[Music]

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.140
Sampling, incubating, plating, transfer,

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.140
and then more incubating.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.100
Laboratory examinations require time,

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.800
and it may take several days to identify the
organisms.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:22.360
Our results show that the other foods were
okay.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.420
But the samples of leftover chicken and the
gravy

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.560
reveal the same bacteria as the stool specimens of
the patients.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.540
For these, too, were thoroughly contaminated
with salmonella typhimurium.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.100
How and when did the chicken and the gravy

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.680
become contaminated with the organisms?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.220
Well, here's one thing we'll have to assume,

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.220
but it's a pretty safe assumption:

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:57.860
one or more of these chickens were contaminated by the salmonella organisms

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.340
on the outside,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.380
and very likely inside.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:08.440
And of course the liver and gizzard are prime suspects.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.540
During the cleaning operation, this cutting
board was undoubtedly contaminated.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:07:13.740
[Music]

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.500
After the chickens were put in the oven,

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.540
the giblets were cooked separately on top
of the stove,

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:29.420
and the cutting board was cleaned.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.660
But what a cleaning it got.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.340
Maybe we should just say that the salmonella
organisms

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:39.020
were more completely distributed over its
surface

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.900
and embedded in the cracks.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:52.080
[Music]

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.800
While the giblets were cooking, a white gravy
was prepared,

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.580
and then the giblets were taken from the stove.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:10.400
Thorough cooking had killed the salmonella
organisms,

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.080
but this good clean food was recontaminated

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.440
on the cutting board as it was chopped.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:54.000
[Music]

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.640
Then these recontaminated giblets were put
into the gravy.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:10.860
[Music]

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.760
This contaminated gravy was not reheated.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.700
It was prepared for serving,

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.940
and on the steam table,

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:20.620
there wasn't enough heat to kill the organisms.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.880
In fact, there's a good chance they began
to grow.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:35.000
[Music]

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.700
The story was much the same with the chicken.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:40.920
Heat killed the salmonella organisms in the
oven,

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.980
but again the unclean cutting board contaminated

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.460
the safe chicken meat as it was carved for
serving.

00:09:49.460 --> 00:10:17.940
[Music]

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:21.380
There wasn't much delay in getting the chicken
served.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:28.800
[Music]

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:31.040
And between the gravy and the chicken,

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.240
we can account for the men who were sick around
midnight or soon after.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:41.720
Those acute cases that occurred later form another chapter in our story.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.020
Here's how the next chapter goes.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:49.360
Food left over from the evening meal

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.670
was saved for the midnight meal,

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:54.690
and here in this lukewarm steam table,

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.880
the salmonella organisms continued to grow.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.080
And to make matters worse,

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:03.290
the cutting board contributed a new bunch
of organisms

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:06.260
as the leftover chicken was prepared for serving.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:09.100
[Music]

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.520
So that by the time the midnight meal was
served,

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.400
the chicken a la king was supporting

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.460
large numbers of salmonella organisms,

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:27.560
enough to make the men on the night watch
so violently ill.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.560
What could have prevented this sickness and
suffering?

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.680
We couldn't know that the chickens were infected.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.600
Look here.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.060
This is a detergent.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.720
This is hot water.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.000
This is a brush.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.180
These are hands.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.820
Put them together.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.880
Use them and get a clean cutting board,

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.140
with all the troublemakers washed off.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:01.720
A good scrubbing immediately after the raw
chicken was prepared

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.620
would have gotten rid of the salmonella organisms.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.880
Of course this applies to our hands and anything
else

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.800
that might be contaminated by contact with
the fowl.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.780
We made some other mistakes too.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:19.260
The leftover chicken should have been put into the refrigerator as soon as possible.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.820
And the gravy.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:26.420
It was cooked before the contaminated giblets
were added.

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:31.340
Thorough cooking after they were added would have killed the salmonella organisms.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:38.600
The air base mess hall accommodated the men in three shifts

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:41.740
of approximately 150 at a time.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.780
Out of some 450 regular personnel,

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:50.920
173 became infected with salmonellosis,

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.960
of which 84 were seriously ill enough to be
hospitalized.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.660
All effected complete recovery

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.520
and were back
on duty within several days to about two weeks.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:15.660
[Music]

